    },
    {
      "id": "how-spring-boot-works",
      "heading": "How Spring Boot Works",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring Boot works based on two major principles:"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 8,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "1-opinionated-defaults",
          "heading": "1. Opinionated Defaults",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Definition: Spring Boot assumes sensible default configurations for most Spring projects so that developers don’t need to set up everything from scratch.",
                "Example: Uses Tomcat as the default embedded server. If no other configuration is specified, Spring Boot automatically configures Tomcat."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 41,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2-customizable",
          "heading": "2. Customizable",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Definition: Though Spring Boot provides default configurations, these can be easily overridden or replaced based on developer needs.",
                "Example: If you prefer Jetty instead of Tomcat, you can change your pom.xml to include Jetty dependencies and exclude Tomcat."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 38,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
